Advanced AC optimization, convex bounds and recovery (@pe-opf-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Convex-Optimization-Boyd-Vandenberghe.lingua#r_54EB992HDGH8YV8BEV5PT5CYHA", #source "../sources/Convex-Relaxation-of-OPF-Low.lingua#r_75K2XQST5PGBNZ7RJ41S3QW08B", #source "../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV", #source "../sources/Power-Grid-Library-OPF-Benchmarks.lingua#r_6AC54N8ECBG43CFWW99NERNWN5", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_3ZT8SH2GTNS3260433VB8A9CHK
**Read:** [Convex Optimization — Boyd and Vandenberghe](../sources/Convex-Optimization-Boyd-Vandenberghe.lingua#r_54EB992HDGH8YV8BEV5PT5CYHA), entire book and substantial proof/calculation work; [Convex relaxation of optimal power flow — Steven H. Low](../sources/Convex-Relaxation-of-OPF-Low.lingua#r_75K2XQST5PGBNZ7RJ41S3QW08B), both entire papers; [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV), whole applicable models/OPF/solver methods; [Power Grid Library — OPF benchmarks and provenance](../sources/Power-Grid-Library-OPF-Benchmarks.lingua#r_6AC54N8ECBG43CFWW99NERNWN5), complete linked report/model and actual case provenance.

Read all of [Convex Optimization — Boyd and Vandenberghe](../sources/Convex-Optimization-Boyd-Vandenberghe.lingua#r_54EB992HDGH8YV8BEV5PT5CYHA), both entire [Convex relaxation of optimal power flow — Steven H. Low](../sources/Convex-Relaxation-of-OPF-Low.lingua#r_75K2XQST5PGBNZ7RJ41S3QW08B) papers, the complete applicable [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV)/[PowerModels.jl — formulations, methods and primary paper](../sources/PowerModels-Methods-and-Formulations.lingua#r_3SDQSM0EXY38699XFME0NQQT2H) formulations and the full [Power Grid Library — OPF benchmarks and provenance](../sources/Power-Grid-Library-OPF-Benchmarks.lingua#r_6AC54N8ECBG43CFWW99NERNWN5) model/report. Select an authorized versioned case and define one actual objective/constraint set before comparing algorithms.

Reconstruct the nonlinear AC problem, a DC approximation and at least one justified convex relaxation. Verify derivatives, balance, each limit and objective units independently on a small case before the larger benchmark. Compare local solutions, valid bounds, recovery/rank or angle conditions and the actual gap. Recovered physical variables must satisfy the original equations; a solver's status or close cost alone is insufficient.

Change a binding network/device condition and predict the effect, distinguishing mathematical marginal values from wider economic or operating conclusions. Explain a failure of exactness, bad initialization, data interpretation or physical feasibility and diagnose it. Report case/solver versions, tolerances, reproducibility, numerical and model limits. The original three-bus example supplies a transparent restricted benchmark, while this study supplies the graduate formulation/proof and physical-feasibility depth.

